## UI design-system discipline

Before making frontend UI, theme, component, Tailwind, CSS, or Storybook changes, use the `ui-design-discipline` skill.

Rules:

- First locate the UI source of truth: tokens, theme config, shared components, docs, Storybook, and lint rules.
- Prefer semantic tokens over raw values.
- Prefer shared component variants over screen-level class recipes.
- Extract repeated list/card/row/header/page-shell patterns into composition primitives.
- Add or update stories for shared UI components that change.
- Add lint/CI guardrails only after the rule is documented.
- Do not redesign broadly when the task is consistency; preserve the existing visual language unless asked otherwise.
